    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d140">

                <pb facs="0217" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File 893.51/630.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the American Chargé
                        d’Affaires</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Extract.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-11-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 1, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Department has been informed by the American group that a loan such as
                    reported in your telegram of October 28 would seriously affect the issue of the
                    loan for currency reform already agreed upon and might seriously interfere with
                    carrying out that reform as well as adversely affecting China’s credit in
                    future. You may informally request of the Chinese Government further details of
                    any proposed loan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
